  "spec_id": "oz-certification-form",
  "description": "Identify the source census tracts, geographic benefit, funding range and project purposes. Preserve whole-text answers and distinct supplied representative context.",
  "children": [
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "Applicant and census tracts",
      "help_text": "View Burden Statement\n\nCertification for Opportunity Zones Preference Points\n\nU.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development \n\nOMB Number: 2501-0044\nExpiration Date: 02/28/2027\n\nType or clearly print the following information.  \n\n**Warning: Anyone who knowingly submits a false claim or makes a false statement is subject to criminal and/or civil penalties, including confinement for up to 5 years, fines, and civil and administrative penalties (18 U.S.C §§ 287, 1001, 1010, 1012, 1014; 31 U.S.C. § 3729, 3802; 24 CFR § 28.10(b)(1)(iii)).  ",
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "field",
          "label": "Applicant Organization:",
          "dat_field": "1-2",
          "required": true,
          "type": "Text",
          "widget": "TextWidget",
          "help_text": "Pre-populated from the SF-424.",
          "json_path": "organization_name",
          "xml_path": "OZ_Certification_Form:OrganizationName",
          "constraints": "minLength 1, maxLength 60",
          "pre_populated": "Pre-populated from the SF-424. Read-only; preview data is illustrative."
        },
        {
          "kind": "field",
          "label": "Assistance Listing number and Federal Program name to which the Applicant is applying:\nInclude the funding opportunity number and name exactly as it appears in the applicable funding opportunity announcement (example: 14.896, Family Self-Sufficiency Program).",
          "dat_field": "1-3",
          "required": false,
          "type": "Text",
          "widget": "TextWidget",
          "help_text": "Pre-populated from the SF-424.",
          "json_path": "federal_program",
          "xml_path": "OZ_Certification_Form:FederalProgram",
          "constraints": "minLength 1, maxLength 120",
          "pre_populated": "Pre-populated from the SF-424. Read-only; preview data is illustrative."
        },
        {
          "kind": "field",
          "label": "Opportunity Zone census tracts",
          "dat_field": "2-0",
          "required": true,
          "type": "Text",
          "widget": "TextAreaWidget",
          "help_text": "Opportunity Zone Census Tract(s),  which the proposed activities/projects will benefit:\nInclude below the full 11-digit census tract number (example: 06067001101). Designated Opportunity Zone Census Tracts can be found at: https://opportunityzones.hud.gov/resources. Select the “CDFI Fund Opportunity Zones Resources” link and then select the “List of designated Qualified Opportunity Zones.”\n\nEnter the Opportunity Zone Census Tract(s) which the proposed activities/projects will benefit. This field is required.",
          "json_path": "census_tracts",
          "xml_path": "OZ_Certification_Form:OZCensusTracts",
          "constraints": "minLength 1, maxLength 1000"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "Geographic benefit",
      "help_text": "Note: Projects which substantially and directly benefit Opportunity Zone Census Tracts, but which do not consist of activities delivered within Opportunity Zone Census Tracts may be considered for competitive preference. If applicable, the respective Federal Agency will clearly define “substantially and directly” in the relevant funding announcement.\n\nEstimated Funding Allocations\n\nEstimate a percentage of the total dollar amount of awarded federal funding that would result in a direct benefit within the Opportunity Zone Census Tracts listed above:",
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "field",
          "label": "The application meets which of the following criteria (please select one):",
          "dat_field": "3-0",
          "required": true,
          "type": "Radio",
          "widget": "RadioWidget",
          "help_text": "The application meets which of the following criteria (please select one). One selection is required.\n\nSolely within — The proposed activities/projects will occur solely within the Opportunity Zone Census Tract(s) listed above.\n\nWithin and other communities — The proposed activities/projects will occur within the Opportunity Zone Census Tract(s) listed above and other communities.\n\nOutside — The proposed activities/projects will occur outside Opportunity Zone Census Tracts, but substantial and direct benefits will accrue within the Opportunity Zone Census Tracts listed above.",
          "json_path": "application_criteria",
          "xml_path": "OZ_Certification_Form:ApplicationCriteria",
          "constraints": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "Funding range and narrative",
      "help_text": "",
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "field",
          "label": "Estimated Funding Allocations",
          "dat_field": "4-2",
          "required": true,
          "type": "Radio",
          "widget": "RadioWidget",
          "help_text": "Estimate a percentage of the total dollar amount of awarded federal funding that would result in a direct benefit within the Opportunity Zone Census Tracts listed above. One selection is required.",
          "json_path": "estimated_funding_allocations",
          "xml_path": "OZ_Certification_Form:EstimatedFundingAllocations",
          "constraints": ""
        },
        {
          "kind": "field",
          "label": "Project support for Opportunity Zones",
          "dat_field": "5-2",
          "required": false,
          "type": "Text",
          "widget": "TextAreaWidget",
          "help_text": "Provide a narrative explaining and/or reference the section in the application that explains how the project will support public and private investment in urban and economically distressed areas, specifically qualified Opportunity Zones (300-word limit):\n\nExample: “The Main Street project described in this application will stimulate economic opportunity and mobility, encourage entrepreneurship, expand quality educational opportunities, and promote workforce development for those families residing within the XYZ Opportunity Zone.”\n\nProvide a narrative explaining and/or reference the section in the application that explains how the project will support public and private investment in urban and economically distressed areas, specifically qualified Opportunity Zones (300-word limit).",
          "json_path": "narrative",
          "xml_path": "OZ_Certification_Form:Narrative",
          "constraints": "minLength 0, maxLength 1500, pattern ^(?!\\s*\\S+(?:\\s+\\S+){300})[\\s\\S]*$"
        }
      ]
    },
