  "notes": [
    "Funding allocation is one exact source range choice. No percentage amount, money question or calculation is invented.",
    "The full census-tract answer remains one 1–1000-character text field; preserve leading zeros and source whole-answer boundaries.",
    "Twenty-two optional purpose boxes use existing exact source Yes/No codes, with no selections inferred from other answers.",
    "Legal certification and warning text remain source-local. Cover and submission context is readonly; all examples are synthetic.",
    "The source PDF’s 300-word narrative limit is represented with an existing string pattern counting whitespace-delimited tokens, alongside the XSD/DAT1500-character bound. No compiler or renderer extension is required.",
    "Optional program strings preserve original XSD minLength1 when present; DAT min0 allows a broader empty lexical form. Absence remains valid."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "Optional name parts use XSD minLength1whenpresent versus DAT min0; source ownership/policy acceptance remains separate.",
    "Review the explicit whitespace-token word-count interpretation; the source gives a word limit but no tokenization algorithm. Punctuation remains within its source word and no inferred policy or semantic parsing is introduced."
  ],
